                                                        JPA

      JDBC : Java Database Connection

     Connect to DB in & Steps
   1. Load The JDBC Driver.
                 ex - Class.forName("com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver");
   2. Establish a Connection.
                 ex - Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/testdb","root","root");
   3. Create a SQL Query.
                 ex - String sql = "INSERT INTO student(name, age) VALUES (?, ?)";
   4. Prepare the Statement
                 ex - PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(sql);
                       5. set Parameters
                                 ex- ps.setString(1, "Meraz"); ps.setInt(2, 25);
                       6. execute the query.
                                 ex- ps.executeUpdate();



JPA Architecture  :

                                                                                       ---------------------                                   -------------------------------------
                                                                                      | Persistence Context | <--------------------            |   Persistence/ Persistence unit   |
                                                                                       ----------------------                        \          ------------------------------------
                                                                                                                                      \                          |
                                                                                                                                    interacts                    | creates
                                                                                                                                          \                      v
                                                                                                                                            \       -----------------------
                                                                                                                                              \     | EntityManagerFactory |
                                                                                                                                                \  ------------------------
                                                                                                                                                 \             |
                                                                                                                                                   \           | creates
                                                                                                ---------------------                                \         v
                                                                                                |  Entity Transaction |<--------------------|           \-------------------
                                                                                                ----------------------                      |-----------| Entity Manager  |
                                                          Database <-------------------------    ---------------------                      | creates    -------------------
                                                                                                |        Query        |<--------------------                    |
                                                                                                ----------------------                                          | manages
                                                                                                                                                                v
                                                                                                                                                          ------------
                                                                                                                                                          |  Entity   |
                                                                                                                                                          -------------



Note:
EntityManagerFactory emf = Persistence.createEntityManagerFactory("myPersistenceUnit"); // "myPersistenceUnit" = persistence.xml me diya hua name

EntityManager em = emf.createEntityManager();

        em.getTransaction().begin();

        Student s = new Student();
        s.setName("Meraz");
        s.setAge(25);

        em.persist(s);
        em.getTransaction().commit();

        em.close();
        emf.close();



 Entity Lifecycle  :


                                                                       -----------------
                                                                       |   REMOVED    |-------------------|
                                                                       -----------------                  |  flush()
                                                                            ^     |                       |
                                                                            |     |                       |
                                                                 persist()  |     | remove()              |                    |------------------------|
                                                                            |     |                       |...................>|                        |
                                                                            |     v                flush()                     |      DATABASE          |
                             -----------------       persist()       -----------------   ------------------------------------->|                        |
                             |   TRANSIENT    | ------------------->|    MANAGED     |   <-------------------------------------|                        |
                             -----------------                       -----------------              find()                     |........................|
                                                                          ^    |
                                                                          |    |  detach()
                                                                 merge()  |    |  close()
                                                                          |    |  clear()
                                                                          |    v
                                                                    -----------------
                                                                    |   DETACHED    |
                                                                    -----------------



Note:
JPA Entity Lifecycle me basically 4 main states hoti hain.

1️⃣ Transient
        - Entity new object hota hai, DB me nahi hota, JPA ko pata bhi nahi.
        - ex : Student s = new Student(); // Transient

2️⃣ Managed (Persistent)
        - Entity Persistence Context ke under hota hai (JPA track karta hai).
        - Changes automatic DB me flush ho sakte hain.
        - ex :  em.persist(s); // Now Managed

3️⃣ Detached
        - Entity pehle managed tha, but EntityManager se disconnect ho gaya.
        - ex : em.detach(s);
               em.close();

4️⃣ Removed
       - Entity ko delete ke liye mark kar diya.
       - ex : em.remove(s); // Removed



Q. Types of Repositories used in spring/spring boot provided by JPA
    - CrudRepository
           |
           v
    - PagingAndSortingRepository
           |
           v
    - JpaRepository
Note: all are interfaces but these are older and new version is : ListCrudRepository and ListPagingAndSortingRepository.





Q. Difference between CrudRepository, JpaRepository and  PagingAndSortingRepository?

.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------.
| Feature                | CrudRepository | PagingAndSortingRepo   |  JpaRepository |
|------------------------|----------------|------------------------|----------------|
| Basic CRUD Operations  |     🟢✔       |         🔴✖           |     🟢✔       |
| Pagination             |     🔴✖       |         🟢✔           |     🟢✔       |
| Sorting                |     🔴✖       |         🟢✔           |     🟢✔       |
| JPA-Specific Methods   |     🔴✖       |         🔴✖           |     🟢✔       |
| Custom Query Methods   |     🔴✖       |         🔴✖           |     🟢✔       |
| Batch Operations       |     🔴✖       |         🔴✖           |     🟢✔       |
'-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------'
